      "mergeID": "5d0c18b47148cb5ffe669ce0",
      "mergedPostDetails": "Annoyingly, if I want to use the newly added optimization-based blocking features to improve my performance, I have to manually re-show countless friends by hand, one at a time. I can't even turn their dynamic bones back on unless I entirely disable that limiter, which is even more frustrating.\n\nI want these things enabled, I just hate how restrictive they currently are, negatively impacting the people who deserve this harsh scrutiny the least: my friends.\n\nAdding a toggle to Performance settings that allows friends to ignore these limits entirely would save a lot of time, hassle and frustration on both our parts, as I trust my friends not to lag my game, and want to see the cool things they make even if they're more intricate. When enabled, dynamic bone update rate is set back to 60 for all users who are friends, and their avatars are never automatically hidden, regardless of their performance impact as a whole.",
      "mergedPostTitle": "\"Bypass Performance Settings\" toggle for Friends",
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "5d00a55d6019092978dad6b2",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "As long as there's an option to not use it.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
